"""Post-run report derived from the complete independent replay; never changes a gate."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
import statistics

ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]
BASE=ROOT/'results/rescope/hex-modal-layout-v2-20260923'
REPORT=ROOT/'results/reports/scientific-report-hex-modal-layout-v2-20260923'


def read(path):return json.loads(path.read_text())


def main():
    rental=BASE/'rental-03';v=read(rental/'local-verification.json')
    r=read(rental/'remote/run-01/result.json');p=read(BASE/'protocol.json')
    cost=read(BASE/'cost-estimate.json');destroy=read(rental/'destruction.json')
    decision=v['decision'];assert decision['complete'] and decision['physics_passed']
    assert decision['development_gates']=={'modal8':True,'modal32':False}
    assert '## 42. ' not in (ROOT/'scientific_report.md').read_text()
    cases=['optimized-q64','optimized-q96']
    medians={(case,path):statistics.median(x['gpu_ms_per_call'] for x in r['timings'] if x['case']==case and x['path']==path)
             for case in cases for path in p['paths']}
    normal=[x for x in v['state_checks'] if not x['capped']]
    maxres=max(x['independent_true_residual'] for x in normal)
    maxstate=max(x['cross_state_relative'] for x in normal)
    maxcomp=max(x['cross_compliance_relative'] for x in normal)
    maxbound=max(x['absolute_l2']/x['limit_l2'] for x in v['product_checks'])
    primary=[x for x in decision['comparisons'] if x['primary']]
    best=[next(x for x in primary if x['case']==case and x['candidate']=='modal8' and x['baseline']=='fused_ai_fp64') for case in cases]
    text=f'''\n\n## 42. Fixed-work GPU comparison: modal8 survives the storage control; warp layout fails\n\n### 42.1 Question, protocol and replacement deployment\n\nDoes modal8 retain its complete-product advantage after adding an ordinary\nsymmetric-half storage control, and does assigning one warp per element improve\nthe modal implementation? This is the separate prospective execution of §41's\nunexecuted study. The user explicitly requested a different instance after the\nfirst host's transfer failure.\n\nThe [final frozen protocol](results/rescope/hex-modal-layout-v2-20260923/protocol.json) and\n[package receipt](results/rescope/hex-modal-layout-v2-20260923/package-receipt.json)\npreserve all numerical and timing rules. The\n[revision audit](results/reports/scientific-report-hex-modal-layout-v2-20260923/revision-review.json)\nchecks **15 unchanged scientific protocol fields, six byte-identical input files\nand nine byte-identical scientific source files** against §41. The five CPU\nsemantic/decision tests pass again. No GPU measurements informed the revision.\n\nTwo create requests were rejected as unavailable offers, with no contracts and\nempty post-error inventories; both HTTP bodies remain in\n[rental-01](results/rescope/hex-modal-layout-v2-20260923/rental-01/create-failure.json) and\n[rental-02](results/rescope/hex-modal-layout-v2-20260923/rental-02/create-failure.json).\nBefore any accepted rental, the prospective quote ceiling was raised from\nUSD 0.60 to USD 0.70/hour because no other currently eligible host met the old\nceiling. The earlier protocol/package remain intact. Instance **52263043**\nthen ran on **machine 20121 in Spain**, different from failed machine 10577,\nat **USD 0.6237037037/hour including allocated storage**. Legacy SCP and\nconnection keepalives completed the package transfer. This does not identify\nthe first host's transfer root cause.\n\nThe study tests nine paths: four donor FP64 paths; dense8/modal8; sym8 with\n300 symmetric-half coefficients; dense32; and modal32 with 24 active lanes\nand eight idle lanes per element warp. Both layouts use block size 128,\nanalytic structured indices, FP64 values and atomic assembly. Modal32 keeps\nthe same 72 coefficients as modal8. The declared dense controls match each\nmodal path's thread ownership.\n\nThe primary cases use q64/q96 physical states on **prolongations of an accepted\ncoarse optimized density field**, not completed optimizations on those fine\ngrids. Independent physical fused-analytic states from §40 supply the identical\nfixed vector for every path. Two non-cubic partial-block random cases, smoke-q4\nand secondary uniform-q64 retain their declared roles. Material floor is\n1e-6; the timed isotropic cubic elements use Poisson ratio 0.3.\n\n### 42.2 Independent numerical outcome\n\nThe GPU run completed in **{r['elapsed_seconds']:.6f} seconds**. Remote and\n[local replay](results/rescope/hex-modal-layout-v2-20260923/rental-03/local-verification.json)\nvalidate **108 retained product records**, each including an action and a zero\ncall immediately following a nonzero call, plus **18 saved states**: nine\naccepted normal solves and nine correctly rejected cap-one controls. All\nfixed-DOF identities and zero-output checks are exact in the tested arrays.\n\nThe largest normal independent true residual is **{maxres:.10e}**,\nmaximum cross-state relative difference is **{maxstate:.10e}**, and\nmaximum cross-compliance difference is **{maxcomp:.10e}**. All normal\nsolutions also pass force-work/element-energy consistency. The largest product\nerror divided by its predeclared hybrid absolute/relative bound is\n**{maxbound:.10e}**. These are compatibility results, separate from timing.\n\nThe unmodified zero-start Jacobi PCG uses requested tolerance 1e-8, independent\ntrue-residual limit 1e-7 and checks every 50 iterations. State times are retained\nas diagnostic records, with only one normal solve per new path/case; they are\n**not** the study's performance samples and cannot provide a new solve-speed\ncomparison against timings from a different rental.\n\n### 42.3 Fixed-work timing and the failed layout hypothesis\n\nAll **297 timing blocks** are retained: 11 randomized rounds per path on three\nlarge cases, 20 complete constrained products per block. CUDA events cover\ninput masking, output zeroing, numerical kernels, atomic or donor assembly and\nfixed-DOF restoration; synchronized host elapsed times are also saved.\nPreparation, context/JIT, transfers, auditing and physical solves are excluded.\nSince each block repeats the identical frozen input and call count, the PCG\nstopping-count mismatch from §40 does not affect this product comparison.\n\n| path | optimized-q64 median ms | optimized-q96 median ms |\n|---|---:|---:|\n'''
    for path in p['paths']:
        text+=f'| `{path}` | {medians[(cases[0],path)]:.6f} | {medians[(cases[1],path)]:.6f} |\n'
    text+='''\n![Complete fixed-work products on the two primary cases](results/reports/scientific-report-hex-modal-layout-v2-20260923/figures/primary-products.png)\n\nWhiskers show observed ranges, not confidence intervals.\n[All 297 timing rows](results/reports/scientific-report-hex-modal-layout-v2-20260923/figures/all-timings.csv),\n[all primary and secondary comparisons](results/reports/scientific-report-hex-modal-layout-v2-20260923/figures/all-comparisons.csv),\nand the [plot source](rescope/hex_modal_layout_v2/export_results.py) are retained.\n\nIn the tables below, R is the median within-round baseline/candidate ratio and\nL is its one-sided 95% paired-bootstrap lower bound (10,000 resamples). The\nmandatory rule is R ≥1.15 and L >1.05. The modal32-versus-modal8 row instead\nrequires R ≥1.10 and L >1.05. A missing self-comparison is marked “—”.\n'''
    for case in cases:
        text+=f'\n**{case}**\n\n| baseline | modal8 R | modal8 L | modal32 R | modal32 L |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n'
        for baseline in p['baselines']+['modal8']:
            values=[]
            for candidate in p['candidates']:
                row=next((x for x in primary if x['case']==case and x['candidate']==candidate and x['baseline']==baseline),None)
                values.extend([f"{row['paired_median_ratio']:.6f}",f"{row['one_sided_95_lower']:.6f}"] if row else ['—','—'])
            text+=f'| `{baseline}` | '+' | '.join(values)+' |\n'
    text+=f'''\n**Modal8 passes all 14 mandatory primary comparisons. Modal32 passes only\nsix of 16 and fails its declared development gate.** The fastest mandatory\nbaseline is fused-analytic at both primary sizes. Its modal8 paired ratios are\n**{best[0]['paired_median_ratio']:.9f}** and **{best[1]['paired_median_ratio']:.9f}**, with\nlower bounds **{best[0]['one_sided_95_lower']:.9f}** and **{best[1]['one_sided_95_lower']:.9f}**.\nThe symmetric-half control does not remove modal8's measured advantage.\n\nModal32 is close to fused-analytic product time and slower than modal8 on both\nprimary cases. It does outperform the dense control with the same warp layout,\nso the transformation still helps within that mapping; it does not improve the\nexisting eight-thread implementation. The experiment rejects this particular\nlayout-improvement hypothesis, not all possible warp-owned implementations.\nNo hardware-counter attribution was attempted. Compiler attributes and\ntelemetry are retained, but alone do not explain the timing mechanism.\n\nThe uniform-q64 secondary case also completes; both candidates' outcomes agree\nwith their primary outcomes. It is not substituted for either primary case.\n\n### 42.4 Interpretation, prior work and remaining publication boundary\n\nThis run supports a **bounded complete-product timing advantage** for modal8\nover all seven mandatory local controls on one RTX 4090. The numerical replay\nis not the basis for that timing statement; the separate randomized timing\nblocks are. Tight within-rental bootstrap bounds do not represent uncertainty\nacross machines, architectures, applications or independently optimized meshes.\nBoth candidates and every declared comparator are reported; no favorable\npost-hoc subset or secondary-to-primary promotion is used.\n\nThe [prior-work limitation](results/reports/scientific-report-hex-modal-layout-v2-20260923/prior-work-use.json)\nremains material. Sym8 is our packed/shared/shuffle implementation of ordinary\nsymmetric-half storage, not a replication of the final Ratnakar et al. journal\nimplementation or a claim to the strongest possible published symmetric code.\nThe previously inspected thesis synopsis establishes prior eight-thread and\nsymmetric-storage work. Its reading status is unchanged, and the final-paper\naccess gap remains open. The catalog remains 98 works, 80 with local full text\nand 18 metadata-only; no new paper is claimed read or downloaded in this run.\n\nThe old profiling decision **`advance_to_charged_campaign=false` remains\nunchanged**. This fixed-input experiment does not measure a complete PCG solve\nor optimizer episode including startup/preparation, and does not repair the\nvariable-stopping-count profiling gate retrospectively. The next questions are\na separately declared fixed-work instrumentation control, a fully charged\naccepted-solve/application comparison, and the unresolved strongest-baseline/\nprior-art audit. No new mathematical basis, end-to-end speedup, systems novelty\nor publication-ready result is claimed.\n\n### 42.5 Collection, destruction, costs and replay\n\n[Collection verification](results/rescope/hex-modal-layout-v2-20260923/rental-03/collection-verification.json)\nchecked all **203 files** in the **1,097,656,387-byte** archive, SHA-256\n`abaae4d9b59e4418c7d3a8a78cf0d1e4c7b5bf352b6ff8962cc36b870175f3d1`.\nThe [instance was destroyed](results/rescope/hex-modal-layout-v2-20260923/rental-03/destruction.json)\nat **{destroy['utc']}**, immediately after byte verification\nand before local numerical replay. A fresh\n[provider inventory](results/rescope/hex-modal-layout-v2-20260923/rental-03/final-instances.json)\ncontains no instances. The failed first host and both unavailable-offer\nrequests remain separate retained evidence.\n\nThe [rate-time estimate](results/rescope/hex-modal-layout-v2-20260923/cost-estimate.json)\nis **USD {float(cost['rate_time_estimate_usd']):.8f}** for\n**{float(cost['seconds']):.6f} seconds**. Combined with §41's failed deployment,\nthe two layout rentals have provisional cost **USD {float(cost['both_layout_rentals_estimate_usd']):.8f}**.\nThe known incomplete ledger subtotal is **USD {float(cost['known_amount_subtotal_usd']):.8f}**.\nTransfer, tax, billed timing, missing older costs and settled invoices remain\nunresolved; account-credit differences are not counted as additional spending.\n\n```sh\nPYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 .venv/bin/python rescope/hex_modal_layout_v2/verify.py \\\n  --inputs results/rescope/hex-modal-layout-v2-20260923/rental-03/remote/inputs \\\n  --run results/rescope/hex-modal-layout-v2-20260923/rental-03/remote/run-01 \\\n  --reference results/rescope/floor-work-20260923/build-02/reference.dylib \\\n  --out /tmp/jpdc-layout-v2-replay-fresh.json\n```\n\nUse a fresh output path. Successful replay preserves modal8's development pass,\nmodal32's failure, and the unchanged failed charged-campaign planning gate.\n'''
    with (ROOT/'scientific_report.md').open('a') as f:f.write(text)
    note=f'''\n\n### 2026-09-23 different-host fixed-work study\n\nThe replacement RTX 4090 run verified all 108 product records, nine normal states and nine capped controls, with 297 randomized timing blocks. Modal8 passes all 14 primary baseline comparisons; ratios versus the fastest mandatory baseline are {best[0]['paired_median_ratio']:.9f} and {best[1]['paired_median_ratio']:.9f}. Modal32 fails (six of 16 comparisons pass), preserving a negative layout result. This is a product-only development result; §40's failed profiling gate and the full-paper access gap remain unchanged. Instance 52263043 was destroyed before local replay. [Report §42](scientific_report.md#42-fixed-work-gpu-comparison-modal8-survives-the-storage-control-warp-layout-fails).\n'''
    for name in ['logbook.md','research_process_review.md']:
        with (ROOT/name).open('a') as f:f.write(note)
    with (ROOT/'invoice_reconciliation.md').open('a') as f:
        f.write(f'\n\n### 2026-09-23 different-host layout study\n\nInstance 52263043: {float(cost["seconds"]):.6f} seconds at quoted compute-plus-storage rate USD 0.6237037037/hour gives USD {float(cost["rate_time_estimate_usd"]):.8f}. Both layout rentals total USD {float(cost["both_layout_rentals_estimate_usd"]):.8f}; known incomplete subtotal USD {float(cost["known_amount_subtotal_usd"]):.8f}. Two rejected offers created no contracts. All rates are provisional, and invoice/transfer/tax reconciliation remains open. [Evidence](results/rescope/hex-modal-layout-v2-20260923/cost-estimate.json).\n')
    print(json.dumps({'section':42,'normal_states':len(normal),'development_gates':decision['development_gates']}))


if __name__=='__main__':main()
